"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. Initially allocated $500,000, the budget was later adjusted to $550,000 and finally approved at $2M by the executive board to cover research, development, and marketing. Key developments include a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research, the addition of five new team members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and a call for R&D proposals to enhance data visualization tools using AI. The project has reached its first major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, led by developer Omar Jensen, with security protocol updates (MFA and encryption) effective from January next year."
